# Pi Tool Guidance

## Permissions Extension

Auto-loaded; replaces `bash` with mode-aware version; blocks sensitive paths.

**Modes**: **Low** (read-only silent) · **Medium** (reversible silent) · **High** (most silent). Switch: `/perm [low|medium|high]` or `--perm-mode <mode>`.

**Always denied**: `dd of=/dev/`, `mkfs`, `eval`, `curl|sh`/`wget|sh`, `rm -rf /~`/`$HOME`/system dirs, `shutdown`/`reboot`/`halt`/`poweroff`, init runlevel changes.

**Sensitive paths**: `.env*`, `~/.ssh/`, `~/.aws/`, `~/.gnupg/`, `~/.kube/`, `~/.docker/config.json`, `~/.config/gh/hosts.yml`, `*.pem`/`*.key`/`*.crt`.

Edit rules: see "AI Dotfiles Source of Truth" below.

# AI Dotfiles Source of Truth

All AI-agent config lives in the `~/.local/share/chezmoi-ai` chezmoi repo — Pi extensions (`dot_pi/agent/extensions/`), permissions, themes, and related templates. Edit files there, never the deployed copies under `~/.pi/` or `~/.config/`.

After edits, apply with `cd ~/.local/share/chezmoi-ai && mise run apply`, then commit in that repo. The live files are generated output; direct edits to them are lost on the next apply.

## zg (zvec-grep)

The zvec-grep MCP search tool runs indexed semantic search (transport: `zg server --stdio`, per `mcp.json`). Routing rules live in `<exploration_gate>` above — this block covers Pi specifics only.

- Semantic discovery → MCP search with `{"root":"<absolute workspace>","query":"<question>"}` (multi-angle: `queries: [...]`, single ranked list: `fuse: true`).
- Exact words, identifiers, paths, regex → `zg query --rg <pattern>` via bash (no index needed).
- Index lifecycle is CLI-side: `zg index` / `zg status`. Never rebuild or drop an index silently — only on explicit request.
- A sufficient source-linked snippet counts as read evidence; open the cited file only when a needed detail falls outside the snippet.